  "transcript": "The bomb knows nothing. No computer, no sensor, no steering, only physics. Gravity pulls it down. Its speed carries it forward. A ballistic curve. Drag slows it down. Wind pushes it off course. The error is set at release. So the intelligence must be in the aircraft. A computer measures speed, altitude, and wind, and solves the trajectory. The CCIP shows where the bomb would land if released now. The pilot moves the marker onto the target and releases. The CCRP reverses the problem. The pilot flies to the target and the computer calculates the release point. Unguided rockets work the same way. No steering, only a predicted impact point. But after release, nothing can be corrected. The impact is a function of the release.",
